# Kak Fit — project rules (match THIS repo)

Coaching platform being pivoted from a Hevy-style solo workout tracker.
Read `.claude/context/` for the full picture (product, design, brand,
conventions, deploy). This rule is the short version; project context wins over
studio defaults.

## Stack
- pnpm workspaces + Turborepo monorepo. Package manager **pnpm@9.15.4**, Node 20.
- **Mobile:** React Native + Expo Router + TS — `apps/mobile` (`@kak-fit/mobile`).
- **Backend:** Next.js hosting tRPC v11 + Better Auth — `apps/web` (`@kak-fit/web`).
- **Shared tRPC routers:** `packages/api` (`@kak-fit/api`).
- **DB:** PostgreSQL + Prisma — `packages/db` (`@kak-fit/db`), Supabase.
- TanStack Query, superjson, AWS Bedrock (AI), Resend/SES, EAS. TS strict.

## Structure & naming
- `apps/mobile/src/{components,lib,hooks}` + `app/` (Expo Router, file-based).
- tRPC: one router file per domain in `packages/api/src/routers/`, composed in
  `src/index.ts` as `appRouter`; export `RouterOutputs` for the app to consume.
- **kebab-case** filenames; React components in `.tsx`; cross-package imports use
  `workspace:*`.
- 2-space indent, double quotes, semicolons — match surrounding code.

## Non-negotiables
- **Theming:** never hard-code colors. Read tokens from `useTheme()` /
  `useThemedStyles()` (`apps/mobile/src/lib/theme.ts`), spacing/radius/typography
  from its scales. Support light + dark. Moving toward the "quiet wealth" palette.
- **Money:** integer **paise** in a ledger — never floats, never a mutable balance.
- **No medical/diagnostic advice** in app copy or logic (`docs/legal.md`).
- Reuse the existing UI primitives (`components/ui.tsx`, `hevy-ui.tsx`, …) before
  adding new ones.

## Checks (run from repo root — ALWAYS db:generate before typecheck)
```
pnpm db:generate      # first, or typecheck shows ~244 phantom errors
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint             # web only
pnpm test             # or: pnpm verify  (typecheck + test)
pnpm test:integration # needs a test Postgres
```

Builds ship via **feature branch → PR → main** (see `.claude/context/deploy.md`).
